WEBVTT

00:18.130 --> 00:21.310
You all right?

00:23.540 --> 00:26.630
I just had a weird dream, and...

00:30.500 --> 00:32.260
Hey, what's wrong?

00:32.260 --> 00:33.230
Are you okay?!

00:33.230 --> 00:34.000
Hey!

02:27.830 --> 02:29.120
It's done.

02:29.410 --> 02:31.040
Thank you.

02:31.530 --> 02:33.110
These are gathering stones, right?

02:33.110 --> 02:35.880
They contain magic power.

02:35.880 --> 02:37.390
I've never seen them before.

02:37.390 --> 02:41.170
There've been a lot of students 
collapsing these past few days.

02:41.560 --> 02:45.090
When I checked on them, they'd all 
been robbed of their magic power.

02:45.640 --> 02:47.040
Does that mean...

02:47.600 --> 02:48.760
Yup.

02:48.760 --> 02:52.240
It seems the attacker is still 
in the College somewhere.

02:53.880 --> 02:57.000
I'm glad you're here, though.

02:57.000 --> 02:58.780
I'll pay you later.

02:58.780 --> 03:00.410
Oh, it's fine.

03:01.080 --> 03:04.150
I happen to have plenty.

03:04.720 --> 03:06.410
Don't be like that.

03:06.410 --> 03:09.090
Being a Sleigh Beggy is your gift.

03:09.480 --> 03:13.660
People need to be paid for 
their abilities and skills.

03:13.660 --> 03:15.320
Abilities...

03:15.320 --> 03:18.810
I've heard something like 
that several times.

03:19.400 --> 03:21.760
It's not necessarily something 
you want to hear, is it?

03:21.760 --> 03:23.970
I'm sorry if it upset you.

03:23.970 --> 03:24.930
N-No.

03:25.900 --> 03:32.550
I think about all the things this body puts
 me through, and what it does for me.

03:32.550 --> 03:34.610
I don't really know what to make of it.

03:35.050 --> 03:39.610
I wonder if I have any other talents.

03:40.590 --> 03:42.840
If this is all I have...

03:45.590 --> 03:49.880
If that's what you want, you should 
look far and wide for what you like.

03:50.280 --> 03:55.130
Talent isn't just lying in front of 
you or handed to you directly.

03:56.150 --> 04:00.120
You're lucky if you find 
it while you're young.

04:01.880 --> 04:02.960
I'll do my best.

04:04.740 --> 04:07.260
Now, take those and let's head back.

04:07.260 --> 04:08.010
Okay.

04:12.270 --> 04:12.940
Huh?

04:12.940 --> 04:13.770
Lucy.

04:13.770 --> 04:14.840
Why are you...

04:14.840 --> 04:17.310
I'll collapse if I leave your side.

04:17.620 --> 04:19.320
That's right.

04:19.320 --> 04:20.440
Principal.

04:20.440 --> 04:21.530
I didn't know you were here.

04:21.990 --> 04:24.220
How are the students?

04:24.220 --> 04:28.230
They're out of mortal danger for now, 
thanks to the gathering stones.

04:28.230 --> 04:30.400
But they all have the same symptoms,

04:30.400 --> 04:33.540
and they're gradually 
losing their magic power.

04:33.540 --> 04:39.530
So long as the attacker is in the College, 
it'll be difficult to continue hiding it.

04:39.960 --> 04:44.130
Thus, I'll inform all students 
of the situation tomorrow.

04:44.490 --> 04:47.120
What shall we do about the 
students who were attacked?

04:47.640 --> 04:51.430
If they aren't culprits, 
we could send them home.

04:51.430 --> 04:53.260
I don't think that'll be an option.

04:53.650 --> 04:57.470
They're entangled with 
the forbidden book now.

04:57.470 --> 05:01.450
They'll be less of a pain all in one place.

05:02.530 --> 05:04.990
Setting aside whether they're "a pain,"

05:05.410 --> 05:11.000
having them here would make it easier 
to manage and assess the problem.

05:12.070 --> 05:13.470
<i>I wonder, though...</i>

05:13.470 --> 05:17.180
<i>Why have they suddenly started collapsing?</i>

05:19.490 --> 05:20.850
Miss Alexandra!

05:20.850 --> 05:21.870
Are you here?

05:26.240 --> 05:28.440
My roommate collapsed!

05:28.970 --> 05:30.610
Another patient?

05:35.360 --> 05:36.620
Give me...

05:37.610 --> 05:38.630
Give me...

05:39.240 --> 05:40.390
Give me...

05:40.880 --> 05:42.430
I need more.

05:42.430 --> 05:43.030
Hey!

05:44.050 --> 05:44.980
Chise!

05:45.730 --> 05:47.640
Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

05:51.230 --> 05:53.340
<i>It's sapping my magic power.</i>

06:16.020 --> 06:17.440
Silly you.

06:18.460 --> 06:21.070
Don't lock eyes with that thing.

06:27.770 --> 06:29.610
No! A burst?!

06:42.700 --> 06:44.410
Elias...

06:44.410 --> 06:46.590
I just saw something...

06:47.080 --> 06:49.260
It took quite a bit of your magic power.

06:49.260 --> 06:51.030
Chise! Are you all...

06:54.630 --> 06:55.830
Lucy...

06:56.240 --> 06:59.090
She doesn't have enough 
left to share with Lucy.

06:59.940 --> 07:03.250
Principal, do you have 
anything high in calories?

07:03.250 --> 07:06.030
Sure, will my snacks do?

07:11.510 --> 07:15.690
So, may I ask what just happened?

07:15.690 --> 07:21.260
The magic book must have stolen Chise's 
magic power through that thing from earlier.

07:21.860 --> 07:24.760
It was probably too inefficient.

07:25.450 --> 07:26.590
Inefficient?

07:27.170 --> 07:31.930
The attacker could have just taken 
all of her magic power and run off.

07:32.610 --> 07:35.300
But for some reason, they didn't.

07:35.720 --> 07:40.330
So the book must have lost 
patience and made a bold move.

07:40.720 --> 07:46.140
Are you suggesting that the 
book is manipulating the user?

07:46.140 --> 07:49.800
Or the user isn't able 
to manage it adequately.

07:50.450 --> 07:53.980
Either way, it might be affecting the user.

07:53.980 --> 07:56.010
Could it be that the attacker...

07:57.320 --> 08:00.670
Doesn't want to kill the sacrifices?

08:01.640 --> 08:06.490
But the first victim, Webster, nearly died.

08:15.130 --> 08:17.470
Lucy, are you okay?

08:17.470 --> 08:19.510
I don't feel too good.

08:19.510 --> 08:20.810
Chise?

08:22.490 --> 08:23.720
Jasmine.

08:24.140 --> 08:25.250
Are you fine?

08:25.250 --> 08:26.920
You feel well enough to be up?

08:26.920 --> 08:28.950
What about you?

08:30.830 --> 08:33.440
My head suddenly feels clear.

08:33.870 --> 08:35.870
And my body seems lighter.

08:41.750 --> 08:44.090
I slept well.

08:43.350 --> 08:45.450
What's gotten into everyone?

08:53.950 --> 08:56.930
Hey, did you see the message 
from the principal?

08:56.930 --> 08:59.220
A forbidden book got stolen.

08:59.220 --> 09:00.140
I did.

09:00.140 --> 09:04.060
You know how there's been a lot of people 
being taken to the nurse's office?

09:04.060 --> 09:07.630
Yeah. I heard it's because the 
attacker's been using the book

09:07.630 --> 09:09.690
to steal magic power.

09:09.690 --> 09:11.680
It's weird, though...

09:11.680 --> 09:13.520
Everyone's been asleep until yesterday,

09:13.520 --> 09:16.730
and suddenly everyone 
wakes up feeling fine today.

09:16.730 --> 09:20.320
My roommate came back this morning, too.

09:20.700 --> 09:24.570
The attacker's still in 
the College, though, right?

09:24.570 --> 09:28.620
Do you think it could be that guy who got 
taken to the nurse's office last night?

09:28.950 --> 09:32.580
I heard he was attacked, too, though...

09:32.580 --> 09:36.260
Which means... one of the teachers, maybe?

09:36.840 --> 09:37.790
Chise.

09:39.480 --> 09:40.650
Elias.

09:42.040 --> 09:44.290
Harvesting?

09:44.960 --> 09:46.570
For a change of pace.

09:47.190 --> 09:50.150
Since you have a tendency to 
pick up on others' malice.

09:52.870 --> 09:54.390
Thank you.

09:56.910 --> 09:59.390
Is this all my fault?

09:59.830 --> 10:03.340
Why did the victims suddenly 
return to normal?

10:03.940 --> 10:05.150
I don't know.

10:05.490 --> 10:08.490
Did they get all the magic they needed?

10:08.490 --> 10:11.290
Or maybe it was too much for them to handle,

10:11.830 --> 10:14.280
and the connection burst.

10:14.740 --> 10:15.630
Burst...

10:19.450 --> 10:21.760
You must be exhausted, too.

10:22.670 --> 10:26.370
I think you've earned a day off.

10:27.500 --> 10:28.220
Yes.

10:36.570 --> 10:38.840
Lucy, want a tomato?

10:40.130 --> 10:40.820
Here.

10:40.820 --> 10:41.620
Hey!

10:42.790 --> 10:45.270
You shouldn't throw food!

10:45.270 --> 10:46.650
Oh... sorry.

10:46.650 --> 10:48.310
Jeez.

10:53.020 --> 10:55.380
By the way, why are you here, Seth?

10:56.000 --> 10:57.740
I'm quite bored, that's all.

10:58.650 --> 10:59.680
I see.

11:00.470 --> 11:02.380
Thanks for the tomato.

11:03.630 --> 11:06.010
Chise! Mr. Ainsworth!

11:06.010 --> 11:07.740
What are you picking?

11:07.740 --> 11:09.830
Tomatoes. Want some?

11:09.830 --> 11:11.410
Yes, please.

11:11.860 --> 11:14.020
Is it all right if I take a few?

11:14.020 --> 11:16.800
I want to feed my familiar.

11:16.800 --> 11:18.280
I suppose it's fine.

11:18.780 --> 11:20.220
Wow, they're huge.

11:20.220 --> 11:21.320
They are.

11:21.570 --> 11:24.550
I didn't get permission to
 harvest them, though.

11:26.140 --> 11:28.820
Hang on, are these actually tomatoes?

11:28.820 --> 11:30.440
They're growing on trees.

11:30.440 --> 11:32.320
I guess that's the cultivar.

11:32.320 --> 11:33.710
Dunno.

11:33.710 --> 11:35.740
Oh, Isaac, want some?

11:35.740 --> 11:38.120
I can't do raw tomatoes.

11:38.420 --> 11:40.450
Hey, where's Rian?

11:40.450 --> 11:42.900
Oh yeah, now that you mention it...

11:44.370 --> 11:46.400
Want some more, everyone?

11:46.400 --> 11:47.130
Yeah!

11:47.130 --> 11:48.610
Yes, please!

11:58.100 --> 11:59.560
You seem happy.

12:03.420 --> 12:04.380
Yeah.

12:04.380 --> 12:07.720
I kinda hope I don't forget this.

12:11.480 --> 12:12.670
<i>I wish...</i>

12:13.370 --> 12:16.330
<i>It's too bad Philomela isn't here with us.</i>

12:16.770 --> 12:18.810
<i>Is it selfish of me to think that?</i>

12:19.240 --> 12:20.590
Chise.

12:20.590 --> 12:22.770
Oh, yeah, coming.

12:24.290 --> 12:26.090
Is there really no way?

12:26.090 --> 12:27.440
Nope.

12:27.440 --> 12:29.800
Boys aren't allowed on the girls'
 floors, or vice versa,

12:29.800 --> 12:31.400
without very good reason.

12:31.750 --> 12:33.320
I just want to make sure she's there.

12:33.320 --> 12:35.030
Nope.

12:35.030 --> 12:39.400
Besides, just because you had a fight 
doesn't make it any less rude of you

12:39.400 --> 12:42.480
to barge in when she's feeling sick.

13:54.660 --> 13:56.180
Where were you?

13:56.450 --> 13:58.890
The first block is about to start.

13:59.350 --> 14:00.230
I'll hurry.

14:14.290 --> 14:15.550
Another one!

14:15.550 --> 14:17.210
Get away from me!

14:17.210 --> 14:18.100
Kevin!

14:17.340 --> 14:19.050
Kevin! Stay away!

14:19.050 --> 14:20.290
I can't!

14:20.290 --> 14:21.960
There're way too many of them!

14:31.260 --> 14:33.940
<i>Those two are together a lot these days.</i>

14:41.590 --> 14:42.630
She...

14:44.440 --> 14:47.960
She waves back at you, I see.

14:48.740 --> 14:51.810
Does your master not?

14:52.870 --> 14:56.270
We used to hold hands often 
when she was little.

14:56.270 --> 15:00.080
I was made to be her caretaker, after all.

15:01.870 --> 15:07.520
But at some point, she started 
refusing to even touch my hand.

15:09.230 --> 15:14.720
I must have lost my purpose.

15:17.210 --> 15:21.490
I think children eventually 
stop needing their parents.

15:21.930 --> 15:22.930
Parents?

15:23.690 --> 15:24.730
No...

15:25.760 --> 15:28.870
She has only a father and a mother.

15:29.540 --> 15:33.080
I've never been given such a role.

15:38.850 --> 15:41.360
I'm her magic teacher,

15:41.360 --> 15:44.640
but I'm also her student,
being taught about being human.

15:45.210 --> 15:48.510
In the beginning, we both 
only had our singular roles.

15:48.980 --> 15:52.020
But now, we are also spouses.

15:53.020 --> 15:56.890
It might be that we have other roles.

15:59.710 --> 16:04.520
But apparently, there's no reason 
to affix ourselves to those roles.

16:07.440 --> 16:08.410
No...

16:09.020 --> 16:13.230
I'm not of an adequate enough 
construction to be much more.

16:13.230 --> 16:15.750
It's not a matter of adequacy.

16:15.750 --> 16:21.150
I mean to say that if you desire it, you 
may also take on the role of a parent.

16:22.160 --> 16:25.210
Though, that's just something 
someone else told me, too.

16:30.950 --> 16:34.220
My desire...

16:38.760 --> 16:40.670
A month and a half...

16:41.350 --> 16:42.270
What?

16:42.560 --> 16:45.050
That's how long it's been 
since the College was closed.

16:45.050 --> 16:47.700
Let us out, already!

16:47.700 --> 16:48.840
Yeah...

16:48.840 --> 16:51.230
The Christmas holiday starts 
the end of next week.

16:51.230 --> 16:52.600
Christmas?!

16:52.830 --> 16:54.600
Hey, are you free on Christmas?

16:54.600 --> 16:55.960
Wanna go out somewhere?

16:55.960 --> 16:57.260
Oh, nice!

16:57.260 --> 16:59.000
There's a new movie coming out!

16:59.000 --> 17:00.610
No one asked you!

17:00.610 --> 17:03.660
It's a gory movie about 
Christmas trees attacking.

17:03.360 --> 17:05.510
What are you making, Chise?

17:06.460 --> 17:07.830
I'm not telling you yet.

17:08.130 --> 17:11.670
You're asking a mage, 
so it must be witchcraft.

17:12.220 --> 17:14.350
I make daily necessities, too.

17:14.670 --> 17:17.950
But, like, they haven't found 
the attacker yet, right?

17:19.140 --> 17:21.900
And there are more golems on patrol now.

17:21.900 --> 17:26.390
It's kinda creepy that no one's been 
attacked this past month, isn't it?

17:26.390 --> 17:28.210
In that case...

17:28.740 --> 17:32.170
Why don't we go looking for the attacker?

17:33.770 --> 17:36.030
It'd be a good way to kill time.

17:36.030 --> 17:38.400
You're too much of a crybaby.

17:38.400 --> 17:41.440
You were nearly sobbing, too!

17:41.440 --> 17:42.580
Do you want to die?

17:46.810 --> 17:51.730
We don't know what they want or 
what kind of person they are.

17:51.730 --> 17:53.970
That's what they call "thoughtless."

17:53.970 --> 17:55.500
Lucy...

17:55.500 --> 17:57.290
Die?

17:57.290 --> 18:00.390
They've just been slowly sucking 
the magic power out of people.

18:00.390 --> 18:03.390
You're all making too much 
of a huge deal of it.

18:04.820 --> 18:06.270
<i>I see...</i>

18:06.270 --> 18:10.670
<i>They don't know about how 
Lucy was the first attacked.</i>

18:10.670 --> 18:13.370
They just happened not to have died.

18:13.370 --> 18:18.120
Not that I'd care if you died.

18:18.120 --> 18:19.010
Yeah?!

18:19.010 --> 18:21.400
Then just shut up and keep sipping your tea!

18:21.400 --> 18:23.040
Cut it out, you two.

18:23.430 --> 18:26.020
Sure, whatever.

18:26.020 --> 18:28.280
Maybe you're the attacker, after all.

18:29.340 --> 18:32.160
The last survivor of the Webster family

18:32.160 --> 18:35.260
would have plenty of reasons 
to hate sorcerers.

18:35.500 --> 18:36.390
Kevin!

18:44.100 --> 18:48.110
There are some things you shouldn't say.

18:49.990 --> 18:54.430
Lucy was with us this whole time.

18:54.910 --> 18:58.120
If she's the attacker, 
people might think Chise,

18:58.120 --> 19:01.100
Isaac and Ryan and I are accomplices.

19:01.590 --> 19:02.400
Zoe...

19:02.400 --> 19:05.280
Sofia and I were with her, too.

19:05.280 --> 19:06.030
Yeah.

19:06.030 --> 19:06.950
What's up?

19:06.950 --> 19:07.770
What's going on?

19:07.770 --> 19:08.360
A fight?

19:08.360 --> 19:09.350
Come on.

19:09.350 --> 19:11.740
He's talking out of his ass
 again. What else is new?

19:11.740 --> 19:13.260
Don't be so harsh.

19:13.260 --> 19:16.100
Kevin, you should apologize.

19:16.100 --> 19:17.710
Seriously?

19:18.010 --> 19:19.240
It was a joke!

19:19.240 --> 19:20.150
Why are you all so—

19:20.150 --> 19:22.150
I don't need you to apologize.

19:25.140 --> 19:27.390
I wouldn't accept it, anyway.

19:27.900 --> 19:29.490
Are you okay?

19:29.490 --> 19:30.640
That was a clean blow.

19:30.640 --> 19:32.000
Nailed his chin good.

19:32.000 --> 19:33.400
Is this really the time?

19:33.840 --> 19:36.530
Hey, what's up with Lucy's family?

19:41.890 --> 19:44.540
Why did you get angry before me?

19:46.250 --> 19:47.130
Oh...

19:47.130 --> 19:47.990
Yeah.

19:48.680 --> 19:53.880
I just realized he says those things 
because he's never seen it before.

19:54.650 --> 19:58.170
Don't go butting into other people's fights.

19:58.650 --> 20:00.670
You're always like that.

20:01.400 --> 20:02.380
Yeah...

20:03.750 --> 20:05.090
So, Chise...

20:05.730 --> 20:07.600
When you say "he's never seen it before,"

20:08.140 --> 20:11.150
that makes it sound like <i>you</i> have.

20:12.600 --> 20:17.420
No, er, well, I just happened to see that.

20:18.580 --> 20:21.230
I haven't said anything yet.

20:24.120 --> 20:25.880
Spill it.

20:41.110 --> 20:42.260
Philomela.

20:45.080 --> 20:46.670
Miss Veronica.

20:47.290 --> 20:49.230
You don't have to get up.

20:49.550 --> 20:52.140
You haven't been feeling 
well lately, have you?

20:52.780 --> 20:55.090
I'm sorry.

20:55.560 --> 20:57.550
Hey, Philomela...

20:57.550 --> 21:00.680
Is there anything you need to tell me?

21:04.920 --> 21:06.270
There isn't.

21:06.810 --> 21:07.620
Oh?

21:08.090 --> 21:09.280
I'm coming in.

21:10.120 --> 21:11.670
Lady Philomela...

21:23.620 --> 21:26.310
You look as pale as I thought you would.

21:26.310 --> 21:28.220
You have to eat, okay?

21:29.310 --> 21:30.300
Yes.

21:48.440 --> 21:49.580
Oh, my.

21:49.890 --> 21:51.040
It's all right.

21:51.040 --> 21:52.720
Let it all out.

21:57.250 --> 22:00.460
<i>What is she thinking?</i>

22:01.340 --> 22:03.470
Miss Veronica...

22:09.510 --> 22:12.570
Never mind.

22:13.290 --> 22:14.460
<i>I'm scared.</i>

22:15.080 --> 22:16.290
<i>I'm scared.</i>

22:17.880 --> 22:19.270
<i>I don't understand.</i>

22:20.200 --> 22:24.270
<i>Everything is terrifying.</i>
